<h2 id="same-day-check">A same-day comparison you can actually record</h2>
<p>Use the same day and device when comparing presentations. Record the app version, selected time window, latest underlying sample, missing readings, displayed score and explanation. Check the price and renewal period offered to your account. If these details differ, a difference between scores is not a fair accuracy test.</p>
<p><strong>Our evidence limit:</strong> we have checked the linked descriptions, not run this protocol across all apps. We do not claim a winner, a measured setup time or a clinical accuracy advantage. The <a href="/stress/apple-watch/#walkthrough">Cortisol+ interface walkthrough</a> shows our product; it is not evidence about competitors.</p>
<p><a href="/resources/apple-watch-app-checklist/">Use the free eight-check app comparison worksheet</a> to keep these observations together. Download the blank CSV and record your own evidence.</p>
<h2>Ask these questions during a trial</h2>
<ol><li>Can I see the underlying readings and when they were recorded?</li><li>Does the app explain missing data and how its baseline is built?</li><li>Can I tell the difference between exercise strain and how I feel mentally?</li><li>Are the features I need included in the price shown to me?</li><li>Can I understand and control data sharing?</li></ol>
<p>Use your own account's current offer to compare prices and renewal periods. We have not reproduced a current paywall for each app and do not present unverified price ranges.</p>
<h2>Which one measures cortisol?</h2>
<p>These wearable stress approaches should not be read as laboratory cortisol measurements. Cortisol+'s number is a model output, and we have not established its clinical accuracy against hormone testing. A branded “cortisol score” does not remove that limitation.</p>
